task: raft-wire-flake (BACKLOG raft-wire-election-flake: "two sightings, enough to act")
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/raft-wire-flake

why: TestRaftWire failed three full gates in two days -- twice on "the
  survivors did not commit after failover" (waitUntil(3000) under
  matrix load 25-30), once on BindException from freePort()'s
  close-then-bind window. Green 3/3 in isolation every time. The
  policy is "no flaky tests in the default gate": fix the timing, or
  tag it Live.

how: fix, not tag -- the test is a real law of the wire. Two changes,
  both in the test: (1) the cluster is built under a retry that
  re-picks ports on BindException (the race is between freePort's
  close and the node's bind; three tries make it a non-event); (2) the
  budgets that assume a quiet box get the box they actually run on:
  election and commit waits scaled to seconds a loaded matrix can meet,
  which cost nothing when the cluster is fast because waitUntil returns
  early. The node's own timeouts (tick 20, election 200, heartbeat 50)
  stay: the law is about the protocol, the budget is about the box.

measure: the suite 10x in isolation before and after under a synthetic
  load (a parallel compile), and the next full gates.
